    {
      "q_id": "neet_che_u05_t02_5",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        1
      ],
      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "For ideal mixing ΔS>0, so ΔG = −TΔS < 0 even though ΔH=0; Statement I is correct. 68% HNO3 in water is a maximum boiling azeotrope (about 393.5 K) and cannot be separated by fractional distillation; Statement II is correct."
    },
    {
